Package: SVclust
Title: Support Vector Clustering Algorithm Package
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    c(person("Lucas", "Scheffer", , "lucasscheffer2001@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Anderson", "Ara", , "ara@ufpr.br", role = c("aut", "ths")))
Description: Implements the Support Vector Clustering (SVC) algorithm of
    Ben-Hur et al. (2001) <https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v2/horn01a.html>.
    SVC maps data to a high-dimensional feature space using a kernel
    function, determines the minimal enclosing hypersphere by solving the
    dual quadratic program with 'osqp', and identifies clusters by checking
    whether the line segments between pairs of points stay within this
    sphere. It offers a median-distance heuristic for the kernel width and,
    for large datasets, the option of applying SVC to a random subset and
    classifying the remaining points with a support vector machine from
    'e1071'.
